.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library parses 5BSD capability bundles (.cap directories) and provides
access to their service declarations, metadata, and executables.
.Pp
A bundle has the structure:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Name.cap/
  etc/
    service.ucl     (one or more UCL service files)
  bin/
    program           (executables referenced by service UCL)
  resources/          (optional application data)
.Ed
.Pp
Each Service.ucl file declares both bundle metadata
.Pq bundle_id, version, author
and a service definition
.Pq program, provides, requires, capabilities .
A bundle may contain up to 32 services.
.Ss Bundle Lifecycle
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
.Fn capbundle_open
parses the bundle directory and all Service.ucl files.
.It
.Fn capbundle_verify
validates integrity: binaries exist, provides are unique, no self-cycles.
.It
.Fn capbundle_resolve_components
resolves each component request against the complete provider set and adds
the resulting dependency edges.
.It
.Fn capbundle_svc_fill_manifest
converts a parsed service to a
.Vt struct svc_manifest
for use by
.Xr serviced 8 .
.It
.Fn capbundle_close
frees all resources.
.El
.Ss Service.ucl Format
Each Service.ucl file is a UCL document with the following keys:
.Pp
Parsing is strict: unknown keys, wrong types, invalid values, and entries
beyond documented limits reject the complete bundle.
.Bl -tag -width "capabilities"
.It Va bundle_id
(string, required for verification)
Reverse-domain bundle identifier.
Maximum 127 characters.
.It Va version
(string, optional)
Version string.
Maximum 31 characters.
.It Va author
(string, optional)
Author name.
Maximum 127 characters.
.It Va program
(string, required)
Executable name relative to
.Pa bin/ .
.It Va provides
(string or array, required for verification)
One or more service names this service provides for the dependency graph.
Maximum 8 entries; names must fit serviced's manifest label limit.
.It Va requires
(string or array, optional)
Service names this service depends on.
Maximum 16 entries, including dependencies added for component providers.
.It Va implements
(array, optional)
Up to 8 objects identifying public component interfaces implemented by the
service.
Each entry requires separate
.Va interface
and semantic
.Va version
strings.
Optional
.Va lifetimes
and
.Va sharing
arrays advertise provider-supported modes.
When omitted they default to process lifetime and exclusive sharing.
A component request resolves only when its requested mode is advertised.
.It Va components
(object, optional)
Maps up to 8 application-local names to component requests.
Each request requires separate
.Va interface
and semantic
.Va version
strings
and may specify a
.Va provider ,
.Va lifetime ,
.Va sharing ,
.Va required
boolean, and provider-defined
.Va options
object.
The supported lifetimes are
.Dq process ,
.Dq job ,
.Dq jail ,
and
.Dq system ;
the default is
.Dq process .
Sharing is independently
.Dq exclusive
or
.Dq shared
and defaults to exclusive.
The provider is normally omitted.
.Fn capbundle_resolve_components
selects the unique exact interface/version implementation from the complete
bundle set.
An explicit provider is a deprecated bundle-local policy pin.
The
.Fn capbundle_policy_open
and
.Fn capbundle_resolve_components_policy
functions instead apply a separately administered version 1.0.0 provider
policy containing interface defaults and per-service component overrides.
Per-service overrides take precedence.
Missing, ambiguous, mismatched, self-provided, or on-demand provider factories
reject resolution.
The resolved provider is added to
.Va requires
and must acknowledge each session with a procdesc or coalition descriptor.
.It Va jail
(object, optional)
Named persistent execution jail with required
.Va name
and absolute
.Va path
and optional
.Va hostname
and
.Va ip4_addr .
.It Va kmod_requires
(string or array, optional)
Up to 8 kernel module names to load before launch for system bundles.
Only letters, digits, period, underscore, and hyphen are accepted; module
paths are rejected.
.It Va arguments
(array, optional)
Literal argument strings appended after the program name in
.Va argv .
No shell parsing is performed.
.It Va environment
(object, optional)
String-valued environment variables.
Names beginning with
.Dq ORACLED_
or
.Dq SERVICED_
and the exact name
.Dq SERVICE_BOOTSTRAP_FD
,
.Dq NETWORKCMP ,
or
.Dq FILESYSTEMCMP
are reserved.
.It Va on_demand
(boolean, optional)
If true, the service is launched on first lookup rather than at boot.
Default: false.
.It Va restart
(string, optional)
Restart policy:
.Dq always ,
.Dq on-failure ,
or
.Dq never .
Default:
.Dq never .
Unknown values reject the manifest.
.It Va stop_timeout
(integer, optional)
Seconds to wait for graceful shutdown before SIGKILL.
Values outside 1\(en300 reject the manifest.
Default: 5.
.It Va max_failures
(integer, optional)
Consecutive rapid restarts before disabling service.
Values outside 1\(en100 reject the manifest.
Default: 10.
.It Va user
(string, optional)
Username for privilege drop.
Maximum 63 characters.
.It Va group
(string, optional)
Group name for privilege drop.
Maximum 63 characters.
.It Va capabilities
(object, optional)
Capability claims to delegate to the service.
See
.Sx CAPABILITIES
below.
.El
.Ss CAPABILITIES
The
.Va capabilities
object may contain the following sub-keys:
.Bl -tag -width "network"
.It Va system
Array of system gate name strings.
These correspond to kernel-level operation gates defined in
.In dev/mac_capability/mac_capability_system_proto.h .
Valid gate names:
.Dq kldload ,
.Dq kldunload ,
.Dq kldstat ,
.Dq reboot ,
.Dq swapon ,
.Dq swapoff ,
.Dq sysctl ,
.Dq kenv ,
.Dq kenv_read ,
.Dq acct ,
.Dq audit .
Unknown names reject the manifest.
.It Va services
Array containing any of
.Dq mount ,
.Dq node ,
.Dq accounting ,
or
.Dq identity .
At most four unique entries are accepted.
These request mac_capability service descriptors rather than activation
tokens.
.It Va paths
Array of absolute filesystem paths (strings).
Maximum 16 entries.
Non-absolute paths reject the manifest.
.It Va files
Array of file capability objects, each with:
.Bl -tag -width "actions" -compact
.It Va path
(required) Absolute filesystem path.
.It Va actions
(optional) Action list: string, array, or
.Dq * .
Valid actions:
.Dq read ,
.Dq write ,
.Dq append ,
.Dq create ,
.Dq delete ,
.Dq stat ,
.Dq lookup ,
.Dq exec ,
.Dq rename_from ,
.Dq rename_to ,
.Dq link ,
.Dq setattr ,
.Dq truncate ,
.Dq connect .
Default if missing or
.Dq * :
all actions.
.El
Maximum 16 entries.
.It Va network
Array of network endpoint objects, each with:
.Bl -tag -width "direction" -compact
.It Va port
Integer port number, range string
.Pq e.g., Dq 80-8000 ,
.Dq *
for all, or
.Dq .<1024
for privileged ports.
Default: all ports (0\(en65535).
Port values exceeding 65535 are rejected.
.It Va ports
Alias for
.Va port .
.It Va protocol
.Dq tcp ,
.Dq udp ,
.Dq hci ,
.Dq l2cap ,
.Dq rfcomm ,
.Dq sco ,
.Dq iso ,
.Dq any ,
or
.Dq * .
Default: any.
.It Va direction
.Dq bind ,
.Dq connect ,
.Dq any ,
or
.Dq * .
Default: bind.
.It Va domain
.Dq inet ,
.Dq inet6 ,
.Dq bluetooth ,
.Dq any ,
or
.Dq * .
Default: inet.
.It Va address
IP address or CIDR notation
.Pq e.g., Dq 192.168.1.0/24 ,
or a BD_ADDR for the Bluetooth domain.
A specific address requires an explicit matching domain.
.It Va prefix
Explicit CIDR prefix length (0\(en32 for inet, 0\(en128 for inet6).
Requires a specific
.Va address .
.El
Maximum 16 entries.
Invalid entries reject the manifest.
.It Va vsock
Array of VSOCK endpoint objects.
Each object accepts a numeric or wildcard
.Va cid ,
a 32-bit
.Va port
or
.Va ports
range, and a bind/connect/any
.Va direction .
Maximum 16 entries.
.It Va jails
Array of jail capability objects or shorthand values.
Each element may be:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
An integer (jail ID).
.It
A string (jail name, maximum 63 characters).
.It
An object with keys:
.Va jid
(integer),
.Va name
(string),
.Va actions
(string or array:
.Dq create ,
.Dq get ,
.Dq set ,
.Dq remove ,
.Dq attach ,
.Dq * ) .
.El
Maximum 16 entries.
Entries with neither jid nor name reject the bundle.
.El
.Pp
For the complete authoritative schema, value defaults, limits, and token
activation model, see
.Xr serviced 5 .
.Ss Verification Checks
.Fn capbundle_verify
performs:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
bundle_id must be present in at least one Service.ucl.
.It
Each service's program binary must exist and be executable.
.It
Each service must provide at least one name.
.It
No duplicate provides within the bundle.
.It
No service may require its own provides.
.El
.Ss Cycle Detection
.Fn capbundle_check_cycles
uses Kahn's algorithm across all provided bundles to detect circular
dependencies in the provides/requires graph.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning int return 0 on success and \-1 on error.
When
.Fa errbuf
is non-NULL, a descriptive error message is written on failure
identifying the bundle name, the failing service, and the specific issue.
.Pp
.Fn capbundle_service ,
.Fn capbundle_svc_provides ,
and
.Fn capbundle_svc_requires
return NULL if the index is out of bounds.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr mac_capability_system 4 ,
.Xr serviced 5 ,
.Xr servicectl 8 ,
.Xr serviced 8
